# Caddy before Cumino's relay (REL-7): HTTPS for relay.cumino.aleclofabbro.it,
# its certificate from the ACME CAs, renewed by Caddy; every request passed to
# the relay on 127.0.0.1:8080, a collect's NDJSON flushed as it comes
# (`flush_interval -1`, MBX-9). Nothing of the requests in the journal
# (CFG-3): no `log` directive in the site, so no access log; and out of the
# default log the two loggers that tell of a request when it fails, with its
# address, its path and its headers: `http.log.error` (a request that ends in
# an error, a 502 while the relay restarts among them) and `http.stdlib` (Go's
# server: a TLS handshake that fails, with its address). What is left: Caddy's
# own faults and its certificates' news. HTTP/1.1 and HTTP/2 only: no HTTP/3
# offered on a UDP port the firewall keeps closed. Installed by provision.sh.
# [Q, C, 25 Nov 2026]

{
	log default {
		output stderr
		exclude http.log.error http.stdlib
	}
	servers {
		protocols h1 h2
	}
}

relay.cumino.aleclofabbro.it {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080 {
		flush_interval -1
	}
}
